Inventory Optimization to predict sales forecasting/stock outs/re-order point/replinishment
    The task is to fine tune the model to achieve the best possible outcome to keep the inventory lean and manage the sales during the seasonal & non-seasonal demands efficiently and meet customer expectations on time.



📊 Dataset Preparation
	•	Load and explore the dataset to understand requirements for inventory optimization.
	•	Remove unnecessary columns that do not contribute to analysis.
	•	Clean the data by handling missing values, trimming extra spaces, correcting data types, and applying necessary transformations.
	•	Use visualizations (plots/graphs) to explore data patterns and relationships.
	•	Detect and handle outliers appropriately for more reliable processing.
🤖 Model Selection
	•	Train and evaluate multiple ML models.
		ML Models - 
		i    Random Forest
		ii   XG Boost
		iii  Linear Regression
		iv   Decision Tree
		v    Support Vector Regression
		vi   LSTM
		vii  K-Nearest Neighbors
		viii Light BGM
	
	•	Establish a baseline by comparing model performance using metrics such as MAE, MSE, RMSE, and R².
	•	Select the model that best fits the dataset and provides optimal predictive accuracy.
